1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,553
Every time your pipeline publishes a snapshot, Nexus keeps the file.

2
00:00:05,103 --> 00:00:10,010
Ten builds a day, for a year, is thousands of files that nobody will ever use again.

3
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,672
The disk fills up.

4
00:00:11,672 --> 00:00:14,823
And one day the repository stops accepting uploads,

5
00:00:14,823 --> 00:00:16,491
in the middle of a release.

6
00:00:17,041 --> 00:00:20,419
The fix is not a person deleting files by hand.

7
00:00:20,419 --> 00:00:24,157
The fix is a job: a task that Nexus runs on its own,

8
00:00:24,157 --> 00:00:25,019
every night.

9
00:00:25,569 --> 00:00:28,594
Today you build that job in the Nexus web page,

10
00:00:28,594 --> 00:00:29,946
one screen at a time.

11
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:31,683
Every click is highlighted,

12
00:00:31,683 --> 00:00:33,228
so you can follow along.

13
00:00:33,778 --> 00:00:34,888
One honest note.

14
00:00:34,888 --> 00:00:37,732
This is a real Sonatype Nexus Repository,

15
00:00:37,732 --> 00:00:38,980
Community Edition,

16
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,506
running on my machine.

17
00:00:40,506 --> 00:00:41,685
Nothing is faked.

18
00:00:41,685 --> 00:00:46,471
The retention in the demo is shortened so you can see the result now.

19
00:00:48,021 --> 00:00:53,141
A snapshot is work in progress. Every deploy makes a new one, with a new time stamp.

20
00:00:53,691 --> 00:00:55,803
Old snapshots are safe to delete.

21
00:00:55,803 --> 00:00:59,131
Nobody should build on yesterday's work in progress.

22
00:00:59,131 --> 00:01:00,603
Releases are different.

23
00:01:00,603 --> 00:01:01,819
Never delete those.

24
00:01:02,369 --> 00:01:06,145
The task is named Maven, delete snapshot. It has two knobs.

25
00:01:06,695 --> 00:01:10,855
Minimum snapshot count: how many of the newest builds to always keep.

26
00:01:11,405 --> 00:01:15,672
Snapshot retention, in days: builds older than this are allowed to go.

27
00:01:16,222 --> 00:01:18,695
A build is deleted only when both agree.

28
00:01:18,695 --> 00:01:19,746
It is old enough,

29
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:22,280
and it is not one of the newest you keep.

30
00:01:22,830 --> 00:01:24,225
A task runs by hand,

31
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:25,828
or on a schedule: once,

32
00:01:25,828 --> 00:01:26,316
hourly,

33
00:01:26,316 --> 00:01:26,735
daily,

34
00:01:26,735 --> 00:01:27,223
weekly,

35
00:01:27,223 --> 00:01:27,780
monthly,

36
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:29,593
or with a cron expression.

37
00:01:30,143 --> 00:01:35,455
Now watch it live. First the problem. Then create the task, run it, and prove it worked.

38
00:01:37,005 --> 00:01:38,552
Start in the terminal.

39
00:01:38,552 --> 00:01:41,929
This is the demo project from lesson ninety-one.

40
00:01:41,929 --> 00:01:43,124
Go to the folder.

41
00:01:43,124 --> 00:01:43,757
Type: CD,

42
00:01:43,757 --> 00:01:44,109
demo.

43
00:01:44,659 --> 00:01:45,480
Set the password from the locked file,

44
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:45,976
the same way as before.

45
00:01:45,976 --> 00:01:47,121
Type: export N E X U S underscore PASS equals dollar,

46
00:01:47,121 --> 00:01:47,380
parenthesis,

47
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:47,467
cat,

48
00:01:47,467 --> 00:01:47,596
tilde,

49
00:01:47,596 --> 00:01:47,726
slash,

50
00:01:47,726 --> 00:01:48,136
dot corp dash pass.

51
00:01:49,286 --> 00:01:50,947
Now publish four snapshots,

52
00:01:50,947 --> 00:01:52,054
one after another,

53
00:01:52,054 --> 00:01:53,162
with a small loop.

54
00:01:53,162 --> 00:01:55,622
It prints the name of each uploaded jar.

55
00:02:03,672 --> 00:02:05,400
Four builds, four uploads.

56
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:06,621
Four jars.

57
00:02:06,621 --> 00:02:08,497
Each has its own time stamp,

58
00:02:08,497 --> 00:02:09,771
and a build number,

59
00:02:09,771 --> 00:02:10,575
one to four.

60
00:02:10,575 --> 00:02:12,183
Nexus keeps all of them.

61
00:02:12,183 --> 00:02:13,993
This is how the pile grows.

62
00:02:14,543 --> 00:02:18,106
Now the browser. Open local host, port eighty-eighty-one.

63
00:02:20,956 --> 00:02:23,836
Log in as admin, with the password from the lab.

64
00:02:33,786 --> 00:02:37,306
The welcome wizard from lesson ninety-one appears again.

65
00:02:37,306 --> 00:02:39,192
Click through it: get started,

66
00:02:39,192 --> 00:02:39,506
next,

67
00:02:39,506 --> 00:02:40,261
then scroll,

68
00:02:40,261 --> 00:02:41,707
acknowledge the notice,

69
00:02:41,707 --> 00:02:42,398
and finish.

70
00:02:42,398 --> 00:02:44,410
Anonymous access stays disabled.

71
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:05,522
Click switch to classic U I. It is the older layout, and every setting is on one page.

72
00:03:06,072 --> 00:03:07,995
A quick tour of the sidebar.

73
00:03:07,995 --> 00:03:09,575
Search finds a package.

74
00:03:09,575 --> 00:03:11,635
Browse lists every repository.

75
00:03:11,635 --> 00:03:13,558
Upload sends a file by hand.

76
00:03:13,558 --> 00:03:15,755
And the gear opens the settings.

77
00:03:15,755 --> 00:03:17,129
Today we use browse,

78
00:03:17,129 --> 00:03:18,296
and the settings.

79
00:03:18,846 --> 00:03:21,577
Click browse. This lists every repository.

80
00:03:23,427 --> 00:03:25,112
Open corp dash snapshots.

81
00:03:26,362 --> 00:03:27,898
Open the version folder.

82
00:03:27,898 --> 00:03:28,666
Four builds,

83
00:03:28,666 --> 00:03:30,522
exactly as we published them.

84
00:03:30,522 --> 00:03:31,610
That is the pile.

85
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:32,378
Remember it.

86
00:03:32,928 --> 00:03:36,640
One more place to remember. Click the gear, and then blob stores.

87
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:41,776
A blob store is where Nexus keeps the real files.

88
00:03:41,776 --> 00:03:43,177
Look at the blob count,

89
00:03:43,177 --> 00:03:44,274
and the used size.

90
00:03:44,274 --> 00:03:45,980
We compare them in a minute.

91
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:50,519
Now the job. Click system, then scroll the menu, and click tasks.

92
00:03:58,269 --> 00:03:59,698
This is the task list.

93
00:03:59,698 --> 00:04:01,386
Nexus already has several,

94
00:04:01,386 --> 00:04:01,970
built in.

95
00:04:01,970 --> 00:04:03,529
Each row shows the name,

96
00:04:03,529 --> 00:04:04,113
the type,

97
00:04:04,113 --> 00:04:04,827
the status,

98
00:04:04,827 --> 00:04:05,671
the schedule,

99
00:04:05,671 --> 00:04:06,516
the next run,

100
00:04:06,516 --> 00:04:07,360
the last run,

101
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:08,658
and the last result.

102
00:04:09,208 --> 00:04:15,032
Click create task. First you choose a type. Nexus has dozens. Type snapshot in the filter.

103
00:04:19,482 --> 00:04:22,149
Two matches. Pick Maven, delete snapshot.

104
00:04:22,699 --> 00:04:27,456
The form. First, the task name. Make it say what it does: delete old snapshots.

105
00:04:31,106 --> 00:04:34,794
Notification email: where Nexus writes if the task fails.

106
00:04:34,794 --> 00:04:36,541
Leave it empty in this lab.

107
00:04:36,541 --> 00:04:37,511
In a real team,

108
00:04:37,511 --> 00:04:39,064
put your team's address.

109
00:04:39,614 --> 00:04:45,566
Repository: choose corp dash snapshots. Never choose a release repository for this task.

110
00:04:46,116 --> 00:04:50,444
Minimum snapshot count: how many of the newest builds to always keep.

111
00:04:50,444 --> 00:04:52,452
One is the smallest safe number.

112
00:04:57,802 --> 00:04:59,130
Snapshot retention,

113
00:04:59,130 --> 00:04:59,689
in days.

114
00:04:59,689 --> 00:05:01,228
The default is thirty.

115
00:05:01,228 --> 00:05:02,976
For this demo I use zero,

116
00:05:02,976 --> 00:05:05,493
so the old builds qualify right now.

117
00:05:05,493 --> 00:05:06,541
In a real team,

118
00:05:06,541 --> 00:05:07,380
keep thirty.

119
00:05:15,530 --> 00:05:20,522
Remove if released: it deletes snapshots whose release already exists. Leave it off.

120
00:05:21,072 --> 00:05:22,160
Task frequency.

121
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,756
Open the list: manual,

122
00:05:23,756 --> 00:05:24,119
once,

123
00:05:24,119 --> 00:05:24,626
hourly,

124
00:05:24,626 --> 00:05:25,062
daily,

125
00:05:25,062 --> 00:05:25,569
weekly,

126
00:05:25,569 --> 00:05:26,150
monthly,

127
00:05:26,150 --> 00:05:27,020
or advanced,

128
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:28,688
with a cron expression.

129
00:05:33,238 --> 00:05:37,996
Choose daily. A quiet hour is best, so Nexus works while nobody is building.

130
00:05:38,546 --> 00:05:41,596
Pick two o'clock in the morning. Then click create task.

131
00:05:55,546 --> 00:05:56,083
Created.

132
00:05:56,083 --> 00:05:57,694
The list shows our task,

133
00:05:57,694 --> 00:05:58,768
scheduled daily,

134
00:05:58,768 --> 00:06:01,252
and its next run: two in the morning.

135
00:06:01,252 --> 00:06:02,997
Nexus does this by itself,

136
00:06:02,997 --> 00:06:03,802
every night.

137
00:06:04,352 --> 00:06:08,939
Do not wait until two. Run it now, by hand. Click the task, and then run.

138
00:06:09,489 --> 00:06:12,006
Nexus asks you to confirm. Click yes.

139
00:06:13,256 --> 00:06:14,746
The status says running.

140
00:06:14,746 --> 00:06:17,352
But this screen does not update by itself,

141
00:06:17,352 --> 00:06:18,407
so click refresh,

142
00:06:18,407 --> 00:06:19,338
in the top bar.

143
00:06:19,338 --> 00:06:20,579
Now it says waiting.

144
00:06:20,579 --> 00:06:22,814
Waiting is the normal resting state.

145
00:06:23,364 --> 00:06:28,057
Go back to the list. Last run now has a time, and last result says O K.

146
00:06:28,807 --> 00:06:32,519
Proof. Back to browse, and open corp dash snapshots again.

147
00:06:33,369 --> 00:06:34,481
One build is left,

148
00:06:34,481 --> 00:06:35,161
the newest,

149
00:06:35,161 --> 00:06:35,840
build four.

150
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,014
Three were deleted.

151
00:06:37,014 --> 00:06:39,300
And the minimum of one was respected.

152
00:06:39,850 --> 00:06:43,626
Now the blob store again. Click the gear, and then blob stores.

153
00:06:45,676 --> 00:06:48,074
The count and the size did not change.

154
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:51,419
Nexus removed the builds from the repository at once,

155
00:06:51,419 --> 00:06:54,069
but the stored files are cleaned up later,

156
00:06:54,069 --> 00:06:55,963
by its own housekeeping tasks,

157
00:06:55,963 --> 00:06:57,604
like cleanup unused blobs,

158
00:06:57,604 --> 00:06:59,497
which is already in your list.

159
00:06:59,497 --> 00:07:02,274
A compact blob store task does the same job,

160
00:07:02,274 --> 00:07:04,609
and you create it with the same form.

161
00:07:04,609 --> 00:07:08,396
So do not expect the disk to shrink the second the job ends.

162
00:07:10,146 --> 00:07:10,380
Last,

163
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:11,364
back to the terminal.

164
00:07:11,364 --> 00:07:12,068
The same facts,

165
00:07:12,068 --> 00:07:13,099
through the Nexus API,

166
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:15,021
so a script or a pipeline can check them.

167
00:07:15,021 --> 00:07:17,036
Count the jars left in corp dash snapshots.

168
00:07:27,886 --> 00:07:28,804
One jar.

169
00:07:29,354 --> 00:07:33,194
And ask for the task itself: its last result, and its next run.

170
00:07:47,844 --> 00:07:49,004
Last result O K.

171
00:07:49,004 --> 00:07:49,657
Next run,

172
00:07:49,657 --> 00:07:51,035
two in the morning,

173
00:07:51,035 --> 00:07:52,341
in universal time.

174
00:07:52,341 --> 00:07:54,372
A job that runs without you.

175
00:07:55,922 --> 00:07:56,832
Your lab task.

176
00:07:56,832 --> 00:08:00,928
Lab ninety-three installs a real Nexus on your virtual machine,

177
00:08:00,928 --> 00:08:03,788
with four snapshot builds already published.

178
00:08:03,788 --> 00:08:05,543
Lab check judges your work.

179
00:08:06,093 --> 00:08:08,230
It lives at git hub dot com,

180
00:08:08,230 --> 00:08:09,756
slash it dash waves,

181
00:08:09,756 --> 00:08:11,511
slash dev ops dash A I,

182
00:08:11,511 --> 00:08:12,350
in academy,

183
00:08:12,350 --> 00:08:12,655
lab,

184
00:08:12,655 --> 00:08:14,563
lab ninety-three dot S H.

185
00:08:15,113 --> 00:08:19,742
One: open the Nexus web page, log in, and look at browse. Four builds.

186
00:08:20,292 --> 00:08:21,534
Two: in settings,

187
00:08:21,534 --> 00:08:22,045
system,

188
00:08:22,045 --> 00:08:22,483
tasks,

189
00:08:22,483 --> 00:08:26,866
create a Maven delete snapshot task for corp dash snapshots.

190
00:08:26,866 --> 00:08:27,962
Keep one build,

191
00:08:27,962 --> 00:08:29,423
retention zero days.

192
00:08:29,973 --> 00:08:33,194
Three: schedule it daily, or weekly, at a quiet hour.

193
00:08:33,744 --> 00:08:39,141
Four: run it by hand. Its last result must say O K, and browse must show one build.

194
00:08:39,691 --> 00:08:41,267
Five: in notes dot text,

195
00:08:41,267 --> 00:08:42,318
write two lines.

196
00:08:42,318 --> 00:08:42,646
Keep,

197
00:08:42,646 --> 00:08:43,237
and when.

198
00:08:43,237 --> 00:08:45,666
Say what you keep and why it is safe.

199
00:08:45,666 --> 00:08:47,307
Say when it runs and why.

200
00:08:47,857 --> 00:08:48,999
Install a J D K,

201
00:08:48,999 --> 00:08:51,068
Maven and python three first,

202
00:08:51,068 --> 00:08:54,350
and keep about three gigabytes of memory free.

203
00:08:54,350 --> 00:08:55,420
Then lab check,

204
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,348
and lab down.

205
00:08:57,898 --> 00:08:59,967
Pass or fail. You need all five.

206
00:09:00,517 --> 00:09:02,907
A Maven delete snapshot task exists.

207
00:09:03,457 --> 00:09:05,761
It ran, and its last result is O K.

208
00:09:06,311 --> 00:09:08,551
Exactly one build is left, the newest.

209
00:09:09,101 --> 00:09:11,255
The task is scheduled, not manual.

210
00:09:11,805 --> 00:09:14,429
Your notes explain what you keep, and when it runs.

211
00:09:14,979 --> 00:09:16,281
To pass, all five.

212
00:09:17,831 --> 00:09:20,668
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

213
00:09:21,218 --> 00:09:25,144
One: lab up, read the task file, and open Nexus in the browser.

214
00:09:25,694 --> 00:09:29,320
Two: create the task, with minimum one and retention zero.

215
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:32,644
Three: set a daily schedule, and run it by hand.

216
00:09:33,194 --> 00:09:37,012
Four: check browse, and write your two lines in notes dot text.

217
00:09:37,562 --> 00:09:41,274
Five: lab check. Then lab down, and prove nothing is left.

218
00:09:41,824 --> 00:09:43,659
Pause the video, and begin now.

219
00:09:45,209 --> 00:09:46,084
Quick check.

220
00:09:46,634 --> 00:09:48,319
Why do snapshots pile up?

221
00:09:48,869 --> 00:09:51,258
Which two settings decide what is deleted?

222
00:09:51,808 --> 00:09:54,219
Why did the blob count not change right away?

223
00:09:54,769 --> 00:09:58,097
Why must the task never point at a release repository?

224
00:09:58,647 --> 00:10:03,020
Enrichment for objective seven, publishing to a repository manager.

225
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:05,640
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

226
00:10:06,190 --> 00:10:09,176
Next: the Maven wrapper, and builds you can repeat.

227
00:10:09,726 --> 00:10:13,054
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
